WEBVTT

01:04.105 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:06.066 --> 01:10.153
The pay-as-you-throw waste system rollout
is causing ongoing confusion.

01:10.236 --> 01:13.031
Fearing they'll have to pay
to dispose of trash,

01:13.114 --> 01:16.743
people are throwing away things
they don't need to.

01:17.243 --> 01:18.912
How could I just throw it away?

01:19.412 --> 01:20.914
I spent money

01:22.165 --> 01:23.666
and sent it off out of respect.

01:24.167 --> 01:27.462
Residents are putting up warning signs
over trash dumping…

01:27.545 --> 01:30.298
It's so hot! Come on, hurry!

01:31.925 --> 01:33.676
It's so hot.

01:33.760 --> 01:34.677
WEDDING INVITATION

01:34.761 --> 01:36.596
Too many home appliances…

01:39.557 --> 01:42.018
I had to rip the limbs off the stuffed toy

01:42.519 --> 01:45.021
so it would fit
in that designated trash bag.

01:45.730 --> 01:47.023
It just felt so wrong.

01:47.607 --> 01:48.983
Don't you even have kimchi?

01:49.067 --> 01:50.777
Everyone knows my engagement is off?

01:50.860 --> 01:53.363
Hey, what in the world do you eat?

01:54.447 --> 01:57.534
-How do you survive on this?
-Life goes on for the living.

01:58.118 --> 02:01.037
That's enough already.
Your mom called me again.

02:01.955 --> 02:03.873
Seems like she's checking if you're alive.

02:04.666 --> 02:07.961
You heard of pain spots?
You know, where you feel pain.

02:09.295 --> 02:11.297
Our organs have pain spots too.

02:12.882 --> 02:14.634
All our internal organs have them.

02:18.596 --> 02:20.265
A broken heart

02:21.057 --> 02:23.017
isn't just a figure of speech.

02:23.601 --> 02:24.978
It actually hurts.

02:25.478 --> 02:26.312
My heart

02:27.939 --> 02:31.192
clenches

02:31.693 --> 02:32.777
painfully.

02:34.362 --> 02:35.363
It's true.

02:35.446 --> 02:38.658
Call your family, you ungrateful brat.

02:40.910 --> 02:44.372
I could no longer meet
my best friend of seven years,

02:45.498 --> 02:47.083
but my best friend of 20 years

02:48.835 --> 02:50.545
was still looking only at me.

02:51.337 --> 02:52.672
Is everything really okay?

02:53.756 --> 02:54.591
How about food?

02:54.674 --> 02:56.843
You must be out of side dishes.

02:57.719 --> 02:58.761
Should I go?

02:59.512 --> 03:00.972
I made a lot of jangjorim.

03:01.681 --> 03:04.100
Even married couples can part ways.

03:04.184 --> 03:06.477
Remarkable people always
live their own way.

03:06.561 --> 03:09.731
By the way… haven't you heard from him?

03:10.565 --> 03:13.026
All right, I won't mention him.

03:13.109 --> 03:14.819
Okay, go on, get some sleep.

03:18.323 --> 03:20.283
Forget what exactly?

03:22.911 --> 03:24.162
Did she say that again?

03:25.496 --> 03:28.708
All she ever says is, "Forget it"
or "You don't need to know."

03:29.959 --> 03:31.628
I wish she'd talk to me.

03:31.711 --> 03:33.296
I wish she'd open up to me.

03:33.379 --> 03:35.173
Well, she thinks she's a grown-up now.

03:35.673 --> 03:37.342
What else is a mother for?

03:38.259 --> 03:40.720
Who's gonna worry about her more than me?

03:41.387 --> 03:43.431
Are you sad
she's not looking for Mom anymore?

03:44.682 --> 03:46.893
She used to only look for me.

03:47.685 --> 03:49.520
Now I'm the only one she doesn't tell.

03:50.438 --> 03:51.773
She's shutting me out.

03:52.357 --> 03:53.191
Traitor.

03:54.067 --> 03:56.069
Where else would you find
a traitor like this?

03:57.195 --> 03:59.489
I'm only telling you, Mom.

04:01.032 --> 04:02.492
This is a secret,

04:03.409 --> 04:05.411
but I like Kim Jeong-geun.

04:06.871 --> 04:08.539
I might even marry him.

04:13.086 --> 04:14.087
Why?

04:14.170 --> 04:16.005
Why do you like Jeong-geun?

04:16.089 --> 04:18.883
He's cute. He's the cutest
in our neighborhood.

04:20.802 --> 04:21.886
Goodness.

04:23.680 --> 04:26.474
Geum-myeong, you're a big girl now.

04:26.975 --> 04:28.810
There's even a boy you like.

04:32.146 --> 04:33.439
But you know,

04:34.649 --> 04:38.444
I wish you'd grow up a little slower.

04:38.945 --> 04:40.154
Just a little slower.

04:40.238 --> 04:41.239
Why?

04:43.157 --> 04:44.993
You're adorable right now.

04:45.618 --> 04:47.120
You're just so adorable.

04:51.499 --> 04:52.333
Geum-myeong.

04:53.042 --> 04:54.502
Even when you grow up,

04:54.585 --> 04:57.130
promise to tell me
lots of your secrets, okay?

04:57.630 --> 05:00.508
Of course, you're my secret keeper.

05:00.591 --> 05:01.759
Really?

05:01.843 --> 05:03.845
You're my best friend, Mom.

05:04.345 --> 05:06.014
Even more than Kim Jeong-geun?

05:07.348 --> 05:08.182
Goodness.

05:09.517 --> 05:12.437
Mom, who's your best friend?

05:12.520 --> 05:15.857
Mine? You're my best friend.

05:16.524 --> 05:19.193
Then who do you like?

05:20.403 --> 05:23.406
I like Yang Gwan-sik.

05:24.115 --> 05:24.949
More than me?

05:25.033 --> 05:28.953
No, you're my favorite
in the whole wide world.

05:29.037 --> 05:31.122
Actually, you're my favorite too.

05:31.622 --> 05:32.457
Really?

05:32.957 --> 05:35.793
Yeah, that's why I bought Popeye
for a snack.

05:35.877 --> 05:39.797
Because you said Popeye was your favorite.

05:39.881 --> 05:41.799
My favorite snack is Apollo.

05:41.883 --> 05:44.552
Oh my. That's why you bought Popeye?

05:44.635 --> 05:47.430
I decided not to buy Apollo

05:47.513 --> 05:49.390
because I love you.

05:51.559 --> 05:52.393
My goodness.

05:52.477 --> 05:53.353
POPEYE

05:53.436 --> 05:54.562
Thank you.

05:54.645 --> 05:56.773
That makes me so happy.

05:57.982 --> 05:59.734
We used to be each other's world.

06:00.735 --> 06:04.030
One left that world,
while the other stayed behind.

06:04.113 --> 06:07.158
What should I make for you later?
I'll make anything.

06:07.950 --> 06:09.077
I want jangjorim.

06:09.160 --> 06:10.703
Jangjorim?

06:10.787 --> 06:16.167
My mom still stayed in the world
where her sweetest secret keeper was.

06:38.940 --> 06:41.317
How can the two of us eat all this?

06:42.527 --> 06:44.070
Where's the fun in eating these?

06:44.612 --> 06:47.865
She works, so it must be hard for her
to visit us over the weekend.

06:48.491 --> 06:49.617
She'd be tired too.

06:50.576 --> 06:54.414
After receiving about a thousand calls
from home asking if I'd eaten,

06:55.373 --> 06:57.291
I felt a strong hunger.

06:59.794 --> 07:01.838
Mom, I'm hungry.

07:02.755 --> 07:04.549
I started craving Mom's cooking.

07:04.632 --> 07:05.591
Baby.

07:06.092 --> 07:08.052
How did you manage to come? How?

07:08.136 --> 07:09.137
I took a vacation.

07:10.012 --> 07:13.182
You should've called me.
It's late already.

07:13.266 --> 07:14.308
I'm hungry.

07:14.892 --> 07:17.603
Yeah, we have food.

07:17.687 --> 07:19.772
I'll whip up some fresh rice in no time.

07:24.152 --> 07:24.986
Baby.

07:25.486 --> 07:27.989
I made a whole pot of jangjorim.

07:28.072 --> 07:31.617
Your dad has been peeling quail eggs
for you since yesterday.

07:32.201 --> 07:34.245
That's right. Chonggak kimchi!

07:34.328 --> 07:36.706
It's well-fermented now.

07:36.789 --> 07:38.791
You like it sour, don't you?

07:38.875 --> 07:42.545
Eun-myeong likes it fresh,
and you like it sour.

07:43.129 --> 07:47.133
I always have to make it separately.
You're just killing me, you are.

07:50.720 --> 07:52.638
The floor's cold. It's cold.

07:59.729 --> 08:01.355
I actually knew it already.

08:02.398 --> 08:07.236
How quiet the house must have been
until just five minutes ago,

08:08.446 --> 08:11.282
and how lonely they must have been.

08:12.158 --> 08:13.534
All right.

08:15.286 --> 08:18.164
If you had called,
I would have gone to the airport.

08:18.789 --> 08:21.375
So you can show up an hour early
like last time?

08:31.719 --> 08:33.804
Go back to sleep after you eat, okay?

08:34.305 --> 08:36.474
Are you feeding a pig?

08:38.768 --> 08:41.771
As a kid, after I fell and cried,
they would give me candy.

08:42.271 --> 08:45.566
Mom, I don't eat broccoli.

08:45.650 --> 08:46.609
It's for digestion.

08:48.361 --> 08:52.615
Let's have some nice,
simple noodles for lunch.

08:52.698 --> 08:53.533
Here.

08:55.117 --> 08:56.536
You call this simple?

08:58.037 --> 09:00.164
Then what does "not simple" look like?

09:00.873 --> 09:04.210
After I recovered from the mumps,
they bought me a pork cutlet.

09:04.293 --> 09:05.962
Come on, you love spicy noodles.

09:10.007 --> 09:11.008
Geum-myeong!

09:12.343 --> 09:13.553
Steamed buns!

09:14.095 --> 09:15.221
You love red beans.

09:16.389 --> 09:18.474
For their heartbroken daughter,

09:19.183 --> 09:21.769
they once again focused
on doing just one thing.

09:21.852 --> 09:23.062
That's right.

09:24.021 --> 09:26.941
Yeah, she just showed up out of the blue.

09:28.818 --> 09:30.778
Obviously, she missed her mom.

09:30.861 --> 09:32.280
That's right, you punk.

09:40.580 --> 09:42.957
Amberjack!

09:43.040 --> 09:44.125
Real amberjack.

09:45.209 --> 09:46.627
Is there fake amberjack?

09:47.128 --> 09:49.839
Against all odds,
they raised me yet again.

09:50.339 --> 09:52.800
Dad, I'm going to gain weight.

09:52.883 --> 09:54.385
Wow, it's amberjack.

09:55.261 --> 09:58.806
They made sure not a pound of me
disappeared from the world.

10:00.057 --> 10:02.393
Really? Okay.

10:03.894 --> 10:06.480
-It's freezing.
-Wow, your brother wants to talk to you.

10:10.401 --> 10:13.195
What? You miss me
now that you're in the military?

10:13.696 --> 10:16.157
"Oh, Sister!"

10:16.240 --> 10:18.868
So you got dumped, huh?
He dumped you, didn't he?

10:18.951 --> 10:21.412
"Oh, Yeong-beom…"

10:23.706 --> 10:26.459
In the fortress
that was both comforting and unsettling,

10:27.418 --> 10:31.797
I slept well and recharged,
just like a bear hibernating for winter.

10:46.187 --> 10:47.021
Geum-myeong.

10:48.648 --> 10:49.774
Geum-myeong.

10:51.776 --> 10:52.610
Geum-myeong.

10:53.653 --> 10:54.904
What is it?

10:56.489 --> 10:57.782
You want to sleep more?

11:00.451 --> 11:02.370
Do you really have to sleep more?

11:03.621 --> 11:04.664
What?

11:05.831 --> 11:06.999
Wake up.

11:07.541 --> 11:09.126
What is it?

11:10.294 --> 11:12.171
Let's go somewhere together.

11:12.254 --> 11:14.173
We can just go later.

11:18.886 --> 11:21.472
Dad, I'm tired!

11:24.850 --> 11:25.851
Go back to sleep.

11:42.743 --> 11:45.663
Why did that thought cross my mind
at that moment?

11:53.587 --> 11:58.300
When I went on trips with Yeong-beom,
I used to jump out of bed at 4:00 a.m.

12:02.430 --> 12:03.973
You knew I'd get up, didn't you?

12:46.640 --> 12:48.434
Why did he put a life jacket on me?

12:59.862 --> 13:03.699
GEUMEUNDONG

13:07.745 --> 13:09.121
Aren't you fishing?

13:11.081 --> 13:13.334
-It's my day off.
-You?

13:13.417 --> 13:15.211
Apparently, there are no clouds.

13:16.504 --> 13:18.631
It's coming now. There it is.

13:21.926 --> 13:23.969
You woke me up to see the sunrise?

13:24.053 --> 13:26.764
You know the new Sunrise Condo
by the Sunrise Restaurant?

13:27.264 --> 13:30.142
You have to pay 30,000 won a night
to see it from there.

13:30.643 --> 13:32.978
But you're seeing it for free,
thanks to your dad.

13:33.062 --> 13:35.731
I'll just pay 30,000 won too.

13:36.315 --> 13:37.149
Pay me, then.

13:40.694 --> 13:42.613
Seeing the sunrise gives you energy.

13:43.197 --> 13:45.658
When I see the sunrise,
I pray no matter what.

13:46.242 --> 13:49.411
For you all to do well,
I just pray every single day.

13:50.830 --> 13:54.750
You see the sunrise every single day?
Are you out here at this time every day?

13:57.920 --> 13:59.380
Don't you want to sleep in?

13:59.463 --> 14:02.424
Who in the world doesn't want to sleep in?

14:03.050 --> 14:05.886
So why is yours the only boat
that sets out so early every day?

14:09.098 --> 14:11.100
How do you live like this every day?

14:12.768 --> 14:14.186
Maybe if I sleep less,

14:14.937 --> 14:16.897
you two can sleep more.

14:19.483 --> 14:20.943
That just wakes me up.

14:21.569 --> 14:23.028
Now that I think about it,

14:23.821 --> 14:27.867
there's never been a day
when Dad woke up later than I did.

14:28.659 --> 14:30.035
Don't you have any hand cream?

14:30.119 --> 14:32.913
Wow, your mom only packed things you love.

14:33.706 --> 14:35.708
The rolled omelet is yours though.

14:35.791 --> 14:38.168
Your mom is so excited to cook for you.

14:40.254 --> 14:41.505
Doesn't it get scary?

14:43.132 --> 14:44.133
It's scary.

14:44.925 --> 14:47.553
There's nothing in the world
as scary as the ocean.

14:48.053 --> 14:51.473
So you just put up with it?
Even if you're scared?

14:52.141 --> 14:54.226
When the wind is fierce and I get scared,

14:54.852 --> 14:56.395
that's what I look at.

14:56.478 --> 14:57.313
The lighthouse?

14:57.396 --> 14:58.564
No.

14:59.398 --> 15:01.775
You see that tiny light over there?

15:03.152 --> 15:04.820
It's the light of a fishing boat.

15:05.821 --> 15:06.780
I just look at that.

15:07.656 --> 15:11.619
Thinking that the boat must feel
lonely and scared like me

15:11.702 --> 15:12.620
makes it less scary.

15:12.703 --> 15:15.205
Thinking about going together
makes it manageable.

15:19.710 --> 15:22.463
Mom and I are always
sailing a boat by your side.

15:23.297 --> 15:24.465
If you're ever hungry,

15:25.799 --> 15:27.801
don't think twice and come home.

15:30.512 --> 15:31.347
Dad.

15:33.223 --> 15:34.475
You're embarrassed, huh?

15:36.060 --> 15:39.939
How do you face the neighborhood?
You already gave out the invitations.

15:40.022 --> 15:43.567
Not at all. I'd be more embarrassed
if you married into that family.

15:44.360 --> 15:47.321
I knew you wouldn't marry him.
I know everything.

15:47.404 --> 15:49.907
You do everything well,
so it'll all go well.

15:50.908 --> 15:52.159
You always say that.

15:53.535 --> 15:55.955
If you say so, does everything go well?

15:56.705 --> 15:57.790
What else can I do

15:59.124 --> 16:00.834
other than say these words?

16:01.418 --> 16:06.715
If you were born into a richer,
more successful family instead of mine,

16:07.967 --> 16:10.719
they would've done everything,
all kinds of things for you

16:10.803 --> 16:12.554
and made sure you never got hurt.

16:12.638 --> 16:14.974
Then don't be my dad in the next life.

16:25.484 --> 16:27.319
Don't ever be my dad again.

16:27.987 --> 16:30.280
-Don't go through all this trouble.
-What trouble?

16:31.699 --> 16:32.533
I'm just happy.

16:32.616 --> 16:35.035
Not once did I have trouble,
thanks to you.

16:35.119 --> 16:36.537
Not even once.

16:36.620 --> 16:41.083
You always give me 120 things
when you only have 100.

16:41.667 --> 16:42.918
How can you give me more?

16:43.752 --> 16:45.754
Don't ever bring up "rich dad."

16:46.380 --> 16:48.590
I wouldn't trade you
for the richest man in the world.

16:51.218 --> 16:52.928
I think that's cured my knees.

16:53.012 --> 16:57.433
Just go to the hospital if you're in pain.
You think cooling patches fix everything?

16:58.017 --> 17:00.894
Seriously, you're so annoying.

17:01.895 --> 17:03.814
You're so annoying.

17:08.652 --> 17:10.404
To be honest, I don't mind…

17:12.406 --> 17:13.615
if you don't get married.

17:14.658 --> 17:17.036
Actually, I like that better.

17:17.119 --> 17:18.328
I'm going to get married.

17:18.412 --> 17:20.956
You're always happy being married.

17:21.040 --> 17:23.042
Why do you keep telling me not to?

17:49.860 --> 17:52.696
That day, I saw a different sun.

17:53.864 --> 17:58.660
Only after my sun,
the first to light up the lonely ocean,

17:59.536 --> 18:01.288
had set forever…

18:03.332 --> 18:08.212
did I realize how warm it was
to be by my dad's side.

18:20.891 --> 18:23.352
Why are you getting off the boat?

18:24.812 --> 18:26.772
I saw the sunrise with my dad.

18:26.855 --> 18:29.024
What about your mom? Isn't she working?

18:29.525 --> 18:31.193
It was just me and my dad.

18:32.319 --> 18:33.695
-Just you two?
-Yes.

18:33.779 --> 18:35.447
-Just the two of you?
-Yes!

18:41.453 --> 18:42.871
Hey, do you study hard?

18:42.955 --> 18:44.289
Dad, do you need help?

18:44.832 --> 18:47.000
You look just like your mom.

18:47.918 --> 18:49.128
Do you study hard?

18:49.211 --> 18:50.796
-I'm actually working.
-Where?

18:50.879 --> 18:52.965
-At a major corporation.
-Which one? Damn it.

18:56.760 --> 18:57.761
Give it to me.

18:58.595 --> 19:02.141
-You're setting sail on a Sunday?
-What's a Sunday for a seaman?

19:02.641 --> 19:04.393
Hey, wear your shoes properly.

19:05.269 --> 19:07.646
Why? Did your wife tell you
to go out again?

19:07.729 --> 19:09.940
Again? Damn it! What do you even know?

19:10.023 --> 19:11.817
What do you know about my family?

19:11.900 --> 19:13.944
Every family has its own way.

19:14.027 --> 19:15.445
He's so disrespectful.

19:16.029 --> 19:17.781
-To someone else's dad.
-Hey!

19:18.282 --> 19:21.451
Hey, he may be a captain now,

19:21.535 --> 19:25.289
but he used to pull in the nets
and cook ramyeon for me, you hear me?

19:25.372 --> 19:28.709
Well, in any case,
you're both captains now, aren't you?

19:29.459 --> 19:30.419
Who said otherwise?

19:32.045 --> 19:34.923
That brat Yang Eun-myeong
broke up with his daughter, right?

19:36.466 --> 19:38.177
That family, seriously.

19:38.677 --> 19:40.929
They are just… Damn it.

19:41.847 --> 19:42.848
My husband

19:42.931 --> 19:44.808
won't be working for you anymore.

19:45.309 --> 19:46.935
He won't be working for you!

19:48.312 --> 19:49.938
Fine. Then don't.

19:50.022 --> 19:51.106
Please don't.

19:58.947 --> 20:01.533
Why's she holding her dad's hand
at her age?

20:02.034 --> 20:03.619
SANDGLASS

20:28.435 --> 20:31.355
Well… what are you up to these days?

20:32.105 --> 20:33.857
Are you running the store properly?

20:38.320 --> 20:41.907
Is it makeup you're selling
or that ridiculous hairstyle?

20:53.752 --> 20:54.586
You know,

20:55.587 --> 20:58.590
If you've got time,
you and I can go out on a boat,

20:59.383 --> 21:00.300
you know,

21:01.343 --> 21:02.594
early in the morning…

21:04.054 --> 21:04.888
Okay?

21:05.889 --> 21:08.892
You know, when the sun rises, we can--

21:08.976 --> 21:10.102
Hire somebody.

21:10.811 --> 21:11.770
What?

21:12.271 --> 21:13.188
I'm busy too.

21:21.863 --> 21:24.366
Do you write to that boy or not? Do you?

21:25.367 --> 21:27.160
If you visit him, you're dead meat.

21:27.244 --> 21:29.496
-He won't see me even if I go.
-So you went?

21:31.456 --> 21:33.000
You did, didn't you? You brat!

21:33.083 --> 21:35.252
I can have him put in military prison!

21:35.335 --> 21:37.129
A friend of mine is a general.

21:43.260 --> 21:44.344
Really,

21:46.179 --> 21:47.139
aren't you ashamed?

21:48.098 --> 21:48.932
You what?

21:49.016 --> 21:51.643
You go around meeting
every woman out there.

21:51.727 --> 21:54.813
It's hilarious that you won't let me
date a single guy.

21:54.896 --> 21:55.772
Goddamn it!

21:55.856 --> 21:58.066
Seriously. What the hell do you know?

21:58.150 --> 21:59.443
Your four kids witnessed it.

21:59.526 --> 22:02.863
Shouting "Goddamn it" all the time
will never make us listen to you.

22:02.946 --> 22:05.198
I should shave your hair off, you little--

22:05.282 --> 22:07.409
Fine, go ahead and shave my head!

22:07.492 --> 22:10.329
You've already ruined my life anyway.

22:10.412 --> 22:13.040
See how you like it
when you're stuck with me forever.

22:18.503 --> 22:20.547
Don't you dare slam that door on me!

22:20.630 --> 22:22.049
It was the wind!

22:27.929 --> 22:29.097
-Listen--
-What?

22:29.181 --> 22:31.683
Too noisy again? Do you own this house?

22:31.767 --> 22:34.353
And what the hell are you even studying?

22:36.229 --> 22:37.481
It's about dinner.

22:37.564 --> 22:38.607
Make whatever.

22:39.107 --> 22:40.067
Actually,

22:40.650 --> 22:43.779
can you eat out before coming home?

22:43.862 --> 22:46.073
Why do you keep eating at home now?

22:46.615 --> 22:48.116
It's uncomfortable for everyone.

22:51.578 --> 22:54.206
Everyone? It's uncomfortable for everyone?

22:54.956 --> 22:56.458
Why is it uncomfortable?

22:57.042 --> 22:59.086
Raise your hand if it's uncomfortable!

23:06.385 --> 23:07.386
T.O. I LOVE EUN-MYEONG

23:07.469 --> 23:09.513
600KM APART, 6MM AT HEART
I WILL ALWAYS WAIT FOR YOU

23:09.596 --> 23:11.431
I DO WAT I WANT
DON'T TELL ME WAT TO DO

23:14.309 --> 23:16.728
You all get to eat white rice,
thanks to me!

23:17.354 --> 23:20.482
You hear me? It's all thanks to me!

23:24.903 --> 23:29.741
Apparently, their kumquat field
is around 10,000 to 17,000 ㎡.

23:30.242 --> 23:33.829
That's quite a big difference,
10,000 ㎡ to 17,000 ㎡.

23:34.329 --> 23:37.207
You know what they say
about the father of that family?

23:37.791 --> 23:41.711
They call him Seogwipo's Yang Gwan-sik.
He's such a devoted husband.

23:42.671 --> 23:45.424
But they actually have
more than a kumquat field.

23:45.924 --> 23:49.886
I heard they own a mountain too.
That family owns a huge mountain.

23:50.679 --> 23:52.431
Do you have a crush on the guy or what?

23:52.514 --> 23:54.766
Why do you keep talking about
the kumquat man?

23:54.850 --> 23:56.685
They have a kumquat field.

23:56.768 --> 23:59.521
They own a mountain. They also have a son.

24:00.272 --> 24:01.314
A public official.

24:02.816 --> 24:05.652
He is 29 and went to a college in Seoul.

24:07.737 --> 24:11.116
To know what a man is like,
you must look at his father.

24:11.199 --> 24:14.161
They learn how to treat their family
from their father.

24:14.244 --> 24:16.246
That's why Eun-myeong's
such a dating expert?

24:17.122 --> 24:19.666
The kumquat man's son
looks like the actor Choi Jae-sung.

24:20.375 --> 24:22.002
You need a handsome man.

24:22.085 --> 24:24.796
You fight a lot less
if you marry a handsome one.

24:25.297 --> 24:28.550
Mom, it's only been a year
since I broke off the engagement.

24:29.092 --> 24:31.511
So what? Is it a crime or something?

24:31.595 --> 24:33.430
The entire neighborhood knows.

24:33.513 --> 24:36.558
Seeing someone else already?
How does that make me look?

24:38.685 --> 24:40.145
So what if they know?

24:43.607 --> 24:45.775
The entire neighborhood knows nothing.

24:54.951 --> 24:57.704
-Why didn't you hand them out?
-Just because.

24:59.539 --> 25:01.249
I had a feeling you'd call it off.

25:01.750 --> 25:02.584
What?

25:03.877 --> 25:05.837
That's how I raised you.

25:14.221 --> 25:15.722
If she can't even ride that,

25:15.805 --> 25:18.350
she'll spend her whole life
in the kitchen.

25:19.184 --> 25:21.645
I want her to have everything.

25:22.145 --> 25:24.189
And I want her to do everything,

25:24.272 --> 25:25.941
every single thing she wants.

25:26.024 --> 25:29.194
I don't want her to set the table.

25:29.277 --> 25:31.404
I want her to be the one to flip it.

25:42.457 --> 25:43.291
Geum-myeong.

25:43.375 --> 25:46.336
You gotta pedal harder. Go on!

25:48.547 --> 25:49.673
Keep having run rolling!

25:50.423 --> 25:51.424
Keep rolling!

25:53.552 --> 25:55.971
Why didn't you flip some tables yourself?

25:56.763 --> 25:58.598
Weren't you angry that you couldn't?

25:58.682 --> 25:59.766
Seven.

26:02.602 --> 26:03.728
Eight.

26:05.480 --> 26:08.692
Why were you always so nice?
Was there a prize for it?

26:08.775 --> 26:11.236
ONE BASKET OF TANGERINES
80 WON FOR TEN

26:13.697 --> 26:15.240
That's 11.

26:17.200 --> 26:19.536
-What?
-Eleven.

26:20.287 --> 26:21.496
It was because of you.

26:21.580 --> 26:22.581
Right.

26:23.290 --> 26:24.165
Because of you.

26:26.710 --> 26:31.381
You were looking at me
with those sweet, twinkling eyes.

26:32.173 --> 26:34.217
How could I just live as I please?

26:38.805 --> 26:42.726
When I held you guys after I gave birth,
this is what I thought to myself.

26:43.393 --> 26:45.895
"From now on, my life will become

26:45.979 --> 26:49.566
the stories my children remember
when they grow up."

26:51.109 --> 26:56.781
"The stories my children will reminisce
about when they come to my funeral."

26:58.450 --> 26:59.701
Once I realized that,

27:01.369 --> 27:04.080
I couldn't bring myself
to live a single day dishonestly.

27:07.417 --> 27:10.378
"The eldest child
of Yang Gwan-sik and Oh Ae-sun."

27:11.129 --> 27:14.549
I think I kind of understood
why that was written on the invitation.

27:15.425 --> 27:17.802
I was their Geum-myeong.

27:18.386 --> 27:19.387
Geum-myeong.

27:20.639 --> 27:25.310
You did nothing wrong. You avoided
a pile of crap because of your luck.

27:27.103 --> 27:29.481
Yeong-beom isn't a pile of crap.

27:29.564 --> 27:31.775
And I know.

27:31.858 --> 27:34.319
You don't have to tell me for me to know.

27:35.737 --> 27:37.280
You're crying on the inside.

27:40.325 --> 27:41.451
When you were a child,

27:41.534 --> 27:44.245
Kim Jeong-geun
didn't want to sit next to you,

27:44.329 --> 27:45.830
and you cried for four days.

27:49.167 --> 27:50.919
How do you even remember his name?

27:51.419 --> 27:52.962
How can I forget it?

27:53.046 --> 27:56.508
It's a secret my secret keeper
told only me.

28:09.187 --> 28:11.398
Think of it as wrapping something precious

28:11.481 --> 28:13.817
and tucking it away
in a warm spot on the floor.

28:13.900 --> 28:14.984
Okay?

28:15.068 --> 28:18.613
Once in a while, it'd be nostalgic
to take it out and look at it.

28:20.740 --> 28:23.827
They say your first love
is meant to be a memory.

28:25.328 --> 28:26.621
How would you know?

28:26.705 --> 28:28.707
You live with your first love.

28:30.792 --> 28:35.088
Live with the joy you had
riding your bike when you were a kid.

28:35.171 --> 28:38.049
It'd be a waste
to miss out on the fun now.

28:40.719 --> 28:41.803
My goodness.

28:43.012 --> 28:45.140
Your hands are still so young.

28:49.269 --> 28:50.937
Just like freshly bloomed petals.

28:51.438 --> 28:52.272
Flower petals.

28:57.235 --> 28:58.737
It'd be a waste for you too.

29:00.029 --> 29:01.614
You should do something.

29:01.698 --> 29:02.824
Write poems.

29:05.118 --> 29:06.369
I write every day.

29:07.537 --> 29:09.330
My poetry collection is over there.

29:10.623 --> 29:14.002
1995 HOUSEHOLD ACCOUNT BOOK
OH AE-SUN

29:16.045 --> 29:20.091
Just like an old garment is turned
into new clothes by a skilled tailor…

29:22.635 --> 29:26.514
I went there like a rag,
but I came back neat and sharp.

30:00.590 --> 30:02.550
She was only here for a few days,

30:03.051 --> 30:05.345
but the house just feels so empty now.

30:07.972 --> 30:10.266
Well, it's always been just the two of us.

30:23.071 --> 30:24.948
Seriously, my goodness.

30:31.955 --> 30:34.541
She should buy things for herself, not us.

30:36.751 --> 30:38.628
She's so caring.

30:39.128 --> 30:40.964
She's just way too caring.

30:41.047 --> 30:43.049
FOR THE FOOD
WRITE YOUR POEM

30:44.300 --> 30:48.388
I received so much,
yet my smallest gesture made us even.

30:49.347 --> 30:51.683
That's how unfair we were.

30:52.684 --> 30:54.143
Goodness, my bones.

30:54.644 --> 30:56.980
The cold makes my bones ache
more and more.

31:00.608 --> 31:01.442
Oh my.

31:03.069 --> 31:06.656
What kind of debt must one owe
to be born a mother?

31:08.116 --> 31:11.911
Our elder went into the water
even past the age of 80

31:12.453 --> 31:15.415
but passed away
without a single intact undergarment.

31:16.332 --> 31:19.669
Her kids chipped away
at the money in their old mom's hands,

31:20.169 --> 31:22.589
yet they couldn't see
it was the price of her life?

31:23.172 --> 31:27.218
They took all from their mother's life
yet cried like devoted children.

31:27.802 --> 31:29.929
But she said she broke even

31:30.013 --> 31:33.391
because even a president might end up
in a prison uniform,

31:33.474 --> 31:38.021
but at least she made a living
on her own until the end.

31:38.104 --> 31:39.105
Oh my.

31:40.189 --> 31:42.734
Not even a dog would steal
a haenyeo's fortune.

31:43.234 --> 31:46.404
The problem lies in one's character,
not one's fortune.

31:46.487 --> 31:49.866
Ae-sun also needs to toughen up.

31:49.949 --> 31:53.411
She feels sorry for everyone,
so she's always broke.

31:53.494 --> 31:55.330
Should I go stop her?

31:55.872 --> 31:56.998
Let her be.

31:57.081 --> 31:58.875
Once we leave this life,

31:58.958 --> 32:01.502
Ae-sun won't have her aunts or friends.

32:01.586 --> 32:05.381
How long can we stand up for her?
Make sure she stands without backup.

32:13.056 --> 32:16.351
Well, at least I don't just take it.
I fight back.

32:17.226 --> 32:21.731
Come on.
Why can't you just live well, just well?

32:22.565 --> 32:25.652
That's why, from the very start,
no one has a fate like yours.

32:26.152 --> 32:28.905
You have a husband
who's a complete fool for you,

32:28.988 --> 32:30.239
a top-university daughter,

32:30.323 --> 32:32.700
and the haenyeo bullies
just gave you a good spot.

32:32.784 --> 32:35.411
-Hey, I'm right here.
-That's not all.

32:35.495 --> 32:38.790
Your sister-in-law
takes care of your parents-in-law.

32:38.873 --> 32:41.209
I wondered when she'd boast about that.

32:41.292 --> 32:44.379
By principle, why should I look after Mom
when she has an older son?

32:44.462 --> 32:46.255
You think you're taking care of her?

32:46.339 --> 32:49.801
You sold off your parents' house
for your business.

32:49.884 --> 32:53.554
Now you're turning your elderly mom
into a maid to look after your children.

32:53.638 --> 32:55.890
"Taking care"? As if.

32:55.974 --> 32:57.600
My mom hates that auntie the most.

32:58.309 --> 33:01.229
When you were a child,
Ae-sun fed you three meals a day.

33:01.729 --> 33:05.233
You should be repaying her
for raising you.

33:05.316 --> 33:07.318
You think Ae-sun's pocket is yours?

33:07.402 --> 33:08.569
What's your problem?

33:08.653 --> 33:10.947
What the hell did you bring?

33:11.698 --> 33:13.408
Why did you bring that mat?

33:16.035 --> 33:18.454
ELVAN WELLNESS MAT

33:25.378 --> 33:27.255
Ae-sun, if Gwan-sik sleeps on that,

33:27.338 --> 33:30.133
it will help his knees heal
and even prevent cancer.

33:30.216 --> 33:34.178
It's actually more expensive,
but I'm not here to profit from family.

33:34.262 --> 33:36.639
I think of you first
when I see something good.

33:37.140 --> 33:40.810
If Gwan-sik places his crooked fingers
on the hot mat, the infrared--

33:42.812 --> 33:45.106
What are you doing? This isn't refundable.

33:46.899 --> 33:48.401
Mother also has back pain, right?

33:49.235 --> 33:51.779
Don't lie and say you bought it for her.

33:51.863 --> 33:53.239
Tell her it's from me.

33:54.282 --> 33:57.243
If I'm spending money,
I might as well boast about it.

33:57.910 --> 34:00.246
You're making me embarrassed.

34:00.747 --> 34:03.416
Go. Just go.

34:05.376 --> 34:08.046
Please come empty-handed next time.

34:10.048 --> 34:13.968
Ae-sun. Your personality
determines your fate, right?

34:15.386 --> 34:17.805
What, are you going to say
my fate is good again?

34:19.057 --> 34:19.891
Look.

34:21.768 --> 34:24.520
You took all my money again today.

34:29.067 --> 34:30.234
Eat one more.

34:31.110 --> 34:32.487
Just one more!

34:33.446 --> 34:36.449
Goodness, what a lousy fate I have.

34:37.742 --> 34:41.746
Who knew I'd be cleaning up after
my grandchild past the age of 60?

34:42.622 --> 34:45.208
Unplug it when you're not using it.
It'll catch fire.

34:45.291 --> 34:46.918
Whenever he catches a cold,

34:47.001 --> 34:49.504
that damn Gyeong-ok blames me
for how I dressed him.

34:49.587 --> 34:52.048
This is worse than looking after in-laws.

34:52.131 --> 34:54.592
-Hey!
-Seo Dong-min!

34:54.675 --> 34:57.053
Stand at attention! Attention, now!

35:00.681 --> 35:03.434
Why sit there
if you're not going to say anything?

35:03.518 --> 35:06.270
Just go. Go home to your wife.

35:06.354 --> 35:08.356
No one's ever been on my side
my entire life.

35:10.024 --> 35:11.818
So, how's your back?

35:12.568 --> 35:14.320
Just mind your wife's back.

35:14.403 --> 35:16.739
Stop using patches and go get acupuncture.

35:16.823 --> 35:18.908
I'll take you there and back.

35:18.991 --> 35:19.867
Yeah, right.

35:19.951 --> 35:21.035
Well, I guess

35:21.911 --> 35:24.789
I've always been biased--

35:24.872 --> 35:27.959
Even a staunch nationalist
wouldn't be as biased as you

35:28.042 --> 35:30.169
in a Korea-Japan match.

35:30.920 --> 35:31.754
Well, listen…

35:32.672 --> 35:34.841
I wouldn't trade you
for the richest man in the world.

35:36.300 --> 35:39.262
I wouldn't trade you
for Korea's most celebrated mother.

35:39.345 --> 35:42.598
Lift your foot!
Why would she want to be your mom?

35:42.682 --> 35:44.475
Doesn't she have a preference?

35:45.601 --> 35:47.812
No daughter-in-law can truly be filial
with a filial son,

35:47.895 --> 35:51.149
and no mother-in-law can tolerate
a son foolishly devoted to his wife.

35:51.232 --> 35:53.526
Even the most celebrated mother
would turn her back on you.

35:56.487 --> 35:57.321
Give it to me.

35:59.699 --> 36:01.200
What's an ungrateful son for?

36:01.701 --> 36:02.952
At least he can do this.

36:03.452 --> 36:05.538
Who said you're an ungrateful son?

36:05.621 --> 36:07.039
Who said that?

36:07.123 --> 36:10.376
Didn't you say you should've raised dogs?
The whole neighborhood knows.

36:10.459 --> 36:12.545
Tell them to stop talking crap.

36:12.628 --> 36:14.297
You've been a filial son too.

36:18.259 --> 36:20.803
I know what it's like to lose parents
but not a child.

36:24.557 --> 36:28.186
Staying alive was the real filial duty.
Who wouldn't know that?

36:47.705 --> 36:49.248
Mom, look.

36:49.999 --> 36:53.336
It's Jong-gu.
Your eldest grandson, Jong-gu, is here.

36:54.003 --> 36:56.339
Grandma, it's me, Jong-gu.

36:58.174 --> 36:59.926
You don't even recognize Jong-gu?

37:00.009 --> 37:02.261
Jong-gu, the stupid idiot.

37:02.929 --> 37:05.181
Mom, you taught Jong-gu to read and write.

37:05.264 --> 37:09.560
He didn't even know his times tables then,
but he grew up to be a card shark.

37:11.896 --> 37:13.689
Sister, you know who I am?

37:14.190 --> 37:15.191
Who am I?

37:15.274 --> 37:16.734
Come on, sister.

37:20.112 --> 37:21.405
Dear me.

37:21.489 --> 37:24.367
My mom once mastered
the Korean and Chinese alphabets,

37:24.450 --> 37:26.202
but she's totally lost her sharpness.

37:26.285 --> 37:29.372
How come it's her mind
that crosses the river first?

37:29.914 --> 37:32.375
-Hello, Ae-sun.
-You're here, Ae-sun.

37:32.458 --> 37:34.085
Come on in.

37:34.168 --> 37:35.628
When did you come all the way?

37:35.711 --> 37:38.756
I thought I might never celebrate
my sister's birthday again.

37:38.839 --> 37:41.008
I came just in case this is the last one.

37:43.010 --> 37:46.055
Grandma, I'm here.

37:46.555 --> 37:49.433
She doesn't know.
She doesn't recognize anyone.

37:49.934 --> 37:53.312
Ae-sun, this is really upsetting me.

37:53.813 --> 37:55.439
She doesn't recognize anyone.

37:56.023 --> 37:57.024
Goodness.

37:58.359 --> 37:59.360
Grandma.

38:02.863 --> 38:05.783
Grandma, I brought you senbei snacks. See?

38:06.742 --> 38:08.911
After you finish your meal--

38:08.995 --> 38:10.204
Of course I know.

38:17.586 --> 38:19.005
Han-gyu's daughter.

38:23.301 --> 38:25.011
My son Han-gyu's daughter.

38:33.936 --> 38:34.812
You…

38:36.063 --> 38:37.982
Have you been well?

39:02.590 --> 39:06.844
So I've always been
Han-gyu's daughter to you?

39:09.472 --> 39:12.850
You forget my name
but remember that I'm Han-gyu's daughter?

39:13.351 --> 39:16.228
Does that make you sad?

39:16.896 --> 39:18.522
No, I'm happy.

39:20.358 --> 39:22.693
I'm so happy.

39:22.777 --> 39:23.652
What is it?

39:24.987 --> 39:26.280
Is something bothering you?

39:27.198 --> 39:29.700
What is it that's bothering you?

39:31.077 --> 39:31.994
What is it?

39:32.078 --> 39:33.788
Is something bothering you?

39:34.538 --> 39:36.040
Is something bothering you?

39:36.665 --> 39:39.293
Nothing's bothering me. Nothing at all.

39:41.087 --> 39:43.672
So what if it is?
Will you buy her another boat?

39:44.382 --> 39:46.717
Just one word
about Han-gyu's daughter's struggle,

39:46.801 --> 39:50.221
and my mom just went ahead
and got her a whole boat.

39:50.721 --> 39:52.681
Mother, I'm struggling too.

39:53.474 --> 39:56.060
Your 60-year-old daughter-in-law
is struggling too.

39:56.143 --> 39:58.604
-Please get me a boat too.
-Stop it.

40:02.149 --> 40:03.067
Grandma.

40:03.150 --> 40:06.946
Do you want to come live with me now?

40:07.446 --> 40:08.280
No.

40:08.989 --> 40:10.658
Come live with us.

40:11.158 --> 40:12.576
I don't want to.

40:13.077 --> 40:15.746
You know Gwan-sik is so caring.

40:15.830 --> 40:18.332
He'll do anything I ask him.

40:19.375 --> 40:20.209
No.

40:20.292 --> 40:21.210
Why not?

40:21.836 --> 40:22.962
Not your house.

40:26.173 --> 40:29.510
Why? Because we are two generations apart?

40:33.556 --> 40:38.894
Grandma, I'll get you dentures
in the spring.

40:39.478 --> 40:41.522
I can cash in my savings plan then.

40:41.605 --> 40:44.984
I'll make sure you get dentures with that.

40:46.360 --> 40:49.113
You? Dentures for me?

40:49.196 --> 40:50.448
Yeah.

40:51.031 --> 40:55.703
You also helped me get new teeth
when I was a child.

40:56.203 --> 40:59.665
Gap-toothed little pup
Don't go near the waters

41:01.208 --> 41:05.796
You'll scare the baby fish
Don't go near the magpie

41:05.880 --> 41:08.007
Caw, caw, they will badmouth you

41:08.090 --> 41:09.008
Let's see.

41:09.091 --> 41:13.220
I won't pull it just yet.
Let me just check if the thread is hooked.

41:13.304 --> 41:16.223
Liar. You say that,
but you'll still pull it out.

41:17.933 --> 41:20.895
You're so smart, just like your dad.
Let's pull that tooth.

41:20.978 --> 41:22.688
That crow is waiting for your tooth.

41:22.771 --> 41:25.191
Wait a moment. Let me count to ten.

41:25.274 --> 41:28.235
It won't hurt. It won't hurt at all.

41:28.319 --> 41:30.613
Pull his tooth first.
His tooth is wobbly too.

41:31.739 --> 41:33.157
Let me see how much it hurts.

41:33.240 --> 41:35.868
His parents can pull his out.

41:40.623 --> 41:43.000
Why do you have a thread on your tooth?

41:43.083 --> 41:44.835
Go get your tooth pulled at home.

41:44.919 --> 41:48.547
You came here to sell hairtail.
Why are you getting a tooth pulled?

41:49.215 --> 41:51.425
Gwan-sik, you do it first.

41:51.926 --> 41:53.219
You try it first.

41:54.512 --> 41:57.640
Can you see if it hurts or not?

42:00.935 --> 42:01.852
Aren't you scared?

42:02.937 --> 42:04.271
So you aren't scared?

42:07.691 --> 42:10.152
My clever little girl.

42:10.736 --> 42:13.781
Where did you pick up
this cute little fool?

42:13.864 --> 42:15.658
Good job.

42:17.952 --> 42:19.328
Huh? Did you pull it?

42:19.411 --> 42:20.788
It didn't hurt, did it?

42:23.249 --> 42:26.585
There comes a season for everyone
when they lose their second tooth.

42:28.879 --> 42:33.801
When did my gap-toothed little pup
grow so big?

42:34.552 --> 42:39.598
The crows won't bring you
new teeth anymore.

42:40.474 --> 42:42.101
I should take care of them.

42:43.477 --> 42:45.312
I know something's bothering you.

42:49.733 --> 42:51.360
I know how you feel.

42:52.736 --> 42:54.697
I know exactly how you feel.

42:56.740 --> 43:01.662
I also want to call out his name loudly
at least once…

43:04.248 --> 43:06.333
and cry my heart out.

43:08.961 --> 43:12.673
After holding it in all my life,

43:14.300 --> 43:16.176
it's now hard for me…

43:19.763 --> 43:22.099
to even say Han-gyu's name.

43:25.394 --> 43:27.229
So I feel even more sorry.

43:33.569 --> 43:34.570
I know

43:35.946 --> 43:37.448
how you feel.

43:39.408 --> 43:41.619
I know exactly how you feel.

44:16.195 --> 44:17.988
"I know exactly how you feel."

44:19.490 --> 44:20.407
Those words

44:21.659 --> 44:24.119
brought Mom to her grandma's lap…

44:27.623 --> 44:29.541
where she cried for a long time.

44:34.129 --> 44:35.673
Why won't you go with her?

44:35.756 --> 44:38.384
She's the daughter
of your favorite son, Han-gyu.

44:39.385 --> 44:41.512
I wonder how much she paid for this.

44:42.471 --> 44:45.557
Why? Do you find it harder
to ask your granddaughter for favors?

44:45.641 --> 44:47.309
Or because of grandson-in-law?

44:47.393 --> 44:50.187
This mat is expensive, isn't it?

44:50.270 --> 44:52.648
You bought her a boat,
so why feel uncomfortable?

44:52.731 --> 44:55.025
Go and enjoy
your granddaughter's food for once.

44:57.903 --> 45:00.114
I couldn't even raise her myself.

45:00.698 --> 45:03.617
I couldn't even feed her a whole croaker
when she was little.

45:04.118 --> 45:05.619
How can I go live there?

45:05.703 --> 45:08.122
You just can't forget
about the damn croakers.

45:08.205 --> 45:11.375
You used to share your croakers
with her all the time!

45:12.543 --> 45:13.377
Oh dear.

45:14.294 --> 45:15.921
Once I get up there,

45:17.881 --> 45:20.676
all that's waiting for me
is Han-Gyu's scolding.

45:22.594 --> 45:26.765
All that's waiting for me
is a scolding from my child.

45:38.193 --> 45:39.778
So warm and cozy.

45:43.615 --> 45:45.909
I think I'm going to sleep well.

46:10.225 --> 46:12.102
Oh my, Mother.

46:12.895 --> 46:14.480
You look like a new bride.

46:15.606 --> 46:20.527
Your children will remember you
by this photo, so pink looks great, right?

46:21.695 --> 46:23.238
Did I live well?

46:26.033 --> 46:27.951
Did I pay off my debt?

46:31.121 --> 46:32.539
You did plenty.

46:33.832 --> 46:35.250
Immeasurably so.

46:37.461 --> 46:39.421
I'm out of breath.

46:40.547 --> 46:42.466
Really out of breath from it all.

46:46.845 --> 46:49.056
You must be gasping for air, right?

46:51.725 --> 46:52.810
So,

46:53.519 --> 46:58.774
was it a picnic or an ordeal?

47:12.621 --> 47:14.039
Definitely a picnic.

47:15.165 --> 47:17.292
I got to see all my children.

47:19.545 --> 47:21.630
It was an unbelievable picnic.

47:36.395 --> 47:37.855
I can't believe it.

47:37.938 --> 47:40.732
KIM CHUN-OK OF GIMHAE KIM CLAN
MAY YOU FINALLY BE REUNITED

47:40.816 --> 47:44.111
Every season in life is full of farewells.

47:45.529 --> 47:46.363
Right?

47:49.658 --> 47:51.285
No one arrives,

47:51.368 --> 47:53.829
and all I see
is people leaving one by one.

47:55.080 --> 47:57.082
Father, Mom.

47:58.500 --> 48:00.627
Your grandmother, your father.

48:12.598 --> 48:13.932
You were right, Mother.

48:15.434 --> 48:18.312
My daughter-in-law was a cut above yours.

48:19.646 --> 48:20.647
Right?

48:26.028 --> 48:29.781
Dear me, I brought three spoons again.

48:32.576 --> 48:34.119
Auntie Chung-su.

48:38.707 --> 48:39.917
My grandmother.

48:41.793 --> 48:45.380
You should've gotten dentures
before you left.

48:47.341 --> 48:48.342
And…

49:00.354 --> 49:04.274
Still, let's leave this world together.

49:07.527 --> 49:08.362
Okay?

49:19.206 --> 49:21.583
We thought we came to the picnic together,

49:22.751 --> 49:24.836
but each had their own tide.

49:25.963 --> 49:28.006
Just as the tides ebb and flow,

49:29.299 --> 49:30.926
some have left,

49:32.469 --> 49:33.679
but for some…

49:35.430 --> 49:36.348
He's here.

49:36.848 --> 49:38.976
The door's open. It's open.

49:39.059 --> 49:41.436
…it was the season
for a new arrival at the picnic.

49:43.355 --> 49:46.316
Oh dear, you must've been through so much.

49:46.400 --> 49:48.986
Eun-myeong, I'm so happy to see you.

49:49.069 --> 49:50.737
Thank you so much, my son.

49:52.447 --> 49:55.283
Why are you just standing there?
Come on in.

49:55.367 --> 49:58.412
I made all kinds of things for you.

49:58.495 --> 50:01.123
You want to give us a salute
before coming in?

50:03.375 --> 50:04.376
Salute?

50:05.627 --> 50:09.047
Wait, why do you have so many things?

50:15.345 --> 50:16.179
Mother.

50:16.263 --> 50:17.681
Fine. Go ahead.

50:23.645 --> 50:25.731
Did you bring something?

50:26.231 --> 50:27.065
What is it?

50:30.902 --> 50:32.112
Hello.

50:32.946 --> 50:33.780
Oh my.

50:38.702 --> 50:39.911
Hi, Hyeon-suk.

50:41.204 --> 50:42.414
You're Bu Hyeon-suk.

50:46.668 --> 50:48.420
My goodness, you guys are…

50:49.921 --> 50:52.299
You guys are still seeing each other.

50:52.382 --> 50:54.176
What now?

50:54.259 --> 50:55.844
What do you want to do?

51:03.226 --> 51:04.227
What…

51:04.853 --> 51:07.522
Why are you putting your hand there?

51:07.606 --> 51:09.900
You're scaring me.
Hyeon-suk, what are you doing?

51:09.983 --> 51:10.817
Mother, Father.

51:10.901 --> 51:12.152
What?

51:12.235 --> 51:13.361
What?

51:14.780 --> 51:15.822
I don't wanna hear it.

51:15.906 --> 51:17.324
You're Grandpa and Grandma now.

51:18.575 --> 51:19.826
Oh my God.

51:24.915 --> 51:26.291
You're Strikey's grandmother.

51:27.459 --> 51:29.002
New sprouts still lift their heads

51:29.669 --> 51:32.089
even in the frozen soil
of the front lines.

51:32.172 --> 51:33.381
These punks…

51:33.465 --> 51:37.677
A winter, as early as their spring,
was on its way.

51:38.678 --> 51:41.807
You little punk,
you were sent to serve your country.

53:07.893 --> 53:09.436
Ms. Yang!

53:22.032 --> 53:23.283
Yang Geum-myeong!

53:25.285 --> 53:26.578
Yang Geum-myeong!

53:26.661 --> 53:28.288
Taiji, don't retire!

53:28.371 --> 53:29.998
Taiji, please!

53:30.707 --> 53:31.875
Taiji!

53:31.958 --> 53:34.085
Geum-myeong!

53:35.545 --> 53:40.842
A glistening winter,
as dazzling as spring, was on its way.

53:44.304 --> 53:47.057
A GLISTENING WINTER

56:33.556 --> 56:38.895
"JUST GET READY AND GO,
RIDE THE MOMENT WITH ALL YOU HAVE."

56:45.693 --> 56:47.946
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang
